## 2. Twelve-round core period derived from the actual controller

Use the prior orbit coordinates x=(j,s,F,w,theta), j in Z3, s and theta binary, F=(F1,F2,F3), w in{0,1,2,3}. Let a=1 exactly when w is0 or3 AND theta=0. The old three controls induce

w'=3-w if a=1, otherwise w;
F'=F+(1,1+a,1+a);
s'=s+F2+a;
theta'=theta+1{w' in{1,3}};
j'=j+(-1)^s' mod3.

Bit additions are XOR. These equations are checked against actual old BRC, with all64 raw fields as well as every quotient atom. The earlier total label Q=(F2+F1,F3+F1)+q(w) remains fixed, q=(00,01,10,11).

If w=1 or2, or (w,theta)=(0,1), H03 never moves the writer. The pair (s,F2) has four-step period and the four contact signs sum to zero, so the entire core returns in four rounds. There are five (w,theta) possibilities of this kind.

The remaining three writer modes cycle as (0,0)->(3,1)->(3,0)->(0,0). Starting at (0,0), the activity flags are1,0,1 and three rounds send (s,F2) to(s+F2+1,F2+1). Six rounds reverse s; twelve restore s,F2 and writer mode. Contact signs in the second six rounds are opposite to the first six, so j also restores. F1 toggles every round and F3 changes with F2; all raw fields and both carried sheets restore after twelve. Other starting points on the three-mode cycle are conjugate shifts.

Thus T^12=I on the stated transport core, and every phase family satisfies Z_(n+12)=Z_n. This does not restore time, audit history, or necessarily the original incoming port. On the384 atoms the exact permutation has60 four-cycles and12 twelve-cycles. This is a finite controllable model, not a universal twelve-step natural period.
